 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Sure, a complementary color is one that is opposite it on the color wheel. For example, blue is complemented by orange yellow. It matters because it gives you deep, rich shadows. If you mix the complementary color with the base color, it cancels out and leaves pure black. Exactly. Use the complementary color for shadows and keep the base color for the lightest parts. Then definitely use it for shadows. You lose nothing if you add a bit of grey. Just mix a little bit of the base color with the same amount of white.",
